<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="Good Shit" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1"><trk><name>Southern Broumovské stěny circuit — Slavný, Špičák, Koruna, Kamenná brána and Kovářova rokle circuit [planning only — not navigation-grade]</name><desc>From Slavný, complete the sandstone circuit through Božanovský Špičák, the Koruna viewpoint, Kamenná brána and the whole Kovářova rokle cave and valley, returning to the same Slavný walking departure. The full circuit is approximately 20.4 km. Red, yellow and green marked paths include a short unmarked Čertovo walking connector; junctions and viewpoint outbacks need careful route attention.

Narrow rocky passages, boulders, steep steps and cliff edges make this a demanding day. Wear sturdy hiking footwear and take care through the narrow cave passage.

Prefer dry, snow- and ice-free daylight. Wet sandstone, mud and ice can make required passages unsafe; check current ground conditions before setting out.

Stay on established walking paths, follow current signs and lawful restrictions, and avoid damaging habitats or disturbing wildlife. Use Kovárna as the existing public walking passage; exploration and climbing require separate permission where applicable.

Postpone the entire itinerary if any required passage is closed, prohibited, unsafe or unusable.

Inherited 450 m ascent, 450 m descent and 360 minutes are approximate planning values without a measured elevation profile; allow extra time for the longer circuit and stops.

Route geometry: © OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL 1.0 — https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright; https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/. Community walking-path mapping combined into this loop. Two-dimensional planning geometry; not a current field survey or navigation-grade.

